The new Mac mini will potentially be unveiled before the iPhone 18 Pro event, which is <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/24/apple-invites-iphone-18-pro-event-soon/">likely to take place on Wednesday, September 9</a>, the report said. Gurman said the new Mac mini will likely be Apple's final new product unveiled before <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/20/tim-cook-stepping-down/">Tim Cook steps down as CEO on September 1</a>, and if so, then it would need to be announced before August ends.<br/>
<br/>
Apple has tested versions of the Mac mini with both M5 and M6 chips, according to Gurman, but it remains unclear which generation of chips Apple ultimately plans to use in the next model. Currently, the Mac mini can be configured with a standard M4 chip or a higher-end M4 Pro chip, 16GB to 48GB of RAM, and up to 8TB of storage.<br/>
<br/>
At the start of May, Apple stopped offering the Mac mini with 256GB of storage for &#36;599, resulting in a 512GB model for &#36;799 becoming the lowest-priced configuration available. Then, in late June, Apple reintroduced the 256GB configuration for &#36;799 after <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/25/apple-just-increased-prices/">raising prices</a> on all Macs and iPads, the Apple TV, HomePods, and the Vision Pro.<br/>
<br/>
